doc/src/ - section entry points and atomic topics
================================================

sections.tex owns the order of the nine paper sections; supplement/ holds
the units of the separate supplementary PDF (../supplement.tex). Each NAME.tex owns
its section heading/label and ordered inputs from NAME/*.tex. Those topic
files contain the prose/subsection headings and include complete figure/table
units. Introduction and conclusion are short standalone sections.

Use ../STRUCTURE.md to find the relevant topic. Preserve complete paragraphs,
environments and equations within a file; use doc-relative input paths.

Examples from the repository root:
    make -C doc -f doc.mk section-results
    make -C doc -f doc.mk part UNIT=results/rq1

The preview imports external references from the last full report when it
exists. It does not rebuild unrelated sections. Finish with make doc to
validate global numbering, bibliography and placement.
